    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d523">

                <pb facs="0597" n="499" sameAs="frus:frus1932v04/pg499"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">393.1111 Baker, Charles/80: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of
                            State to the Consul General at Shanghai (Cunningham)</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1932-04-23T14:00:00-05:00">April 23, 1932—2 p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>151. For the Minister. Your April 23, noon. The Department is gratified at the
                    energetic presentation made by you of the Baker case to Chinese authorities at Nanking.</p>
                <p>Referring to paragraph 8 of your telegram under reference Department grants you
                    authorization requested to delay assigning special officer to watch this
                    case.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Castle</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
